title: Hjalmar Schacht has resigned!
view-if: year = 1930 and month >= 3 and hjalmar_plot != "successful"
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
tags: event

= Objections

Hjalmar Schacht, president of the Reichsbank has resigned from his position.

After major disagreements with the government concerning the young plan, which he sees as national economic slavery he has resigned out of protest! Replacing him is ex DVP member Hans Luther.

Despite his resignation, he still holds considerable of informal and economic influence, especially regarding the budget and currency stability. We still cannot enact our monetary policies even if Luther supported us.

If only their was a way to get rid of all this...

- @Carl: Carl Severing proposes an idea.

@Carl
view-if: severing_advisor = 1 and hjalmar_plot != "successful" and hjalmar_plot <= 0

= The Death of Hjalmar Schacht

With Carl Severing's spies having been thoroughly tested against enemies of the republic, Carl vows that his operatives will perform this duty without being caught.

Should we agree?

-@root: This is preposterous!
-@hjalmar: Perhaps extreme times, call for extreme measures.

@hjalmar
view-if: hjalmar_plot != "successful" or hjalmar_plot != "failed"
on-arrival: hjalmar_plot +=10; plot_target = "hjalmar"
go-to: spies

With the Reichsbank being controlled by a known reactionary who collaborated with the Nazis. The only way for us to push out our fiscal reforms is by his Death.

Operation Reversed Scale has commenced. 

@spies
on-arrival: spy_network +=3 if spy_network < 9; plot_strength = spy_network; assassination_partners = "Spies"; resources +=1; month_actions +=1; paramilitaries_timer = 2; {!
new_hire()
!}

Using our own network of <span style="color:rgb(0, 0, 0);">**spies**</span> to carry this out instead. This is the slowest option, but perhaps with more funding we can change that.